# Vitest Testing Guidelines

## 1. Core Testing Principles

### 1.1 Testing Philosophy
- Test behavior, not implementation
- Focus on user interactions and outcomes
- Maintain test isolation
- Keep tests simple and maintainable
- Follow AAA pattern (Arrange, Act, Assert)

### 1.2 Test Structure
```tsx
// Example of ideal test structure
describe("ComponentName", () => {
  // Setup
  beforeEach(() => {
    // Common setup code
  });

  // Cleanup
  afterEach(() => {
    // Cleanup code
  });

  // Test cases
  it("should [expected behavior]", () => {
    // Arrange
    // Act
    // Assert
  });
});
```

## 2. Component Testing

### 2.1 Basic Component Tests
```tsx
import { render, screen } from "@testing-library/react";
import Button from "./Button";

describe("Button", () => {
  it("renders with correct text", () => {
    render(<Button>Click me</Button>);
    expect(screen.getByText("Click me")).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it("handles disabled state", () => {
    render(<Button disabled>Click me</Button>);
    expect(screen.getByRole("button")).toBeDisabled();
  });
});
```

### 2.2 Event Handling Tests
```tsx
it("handles click events", async () => {
  const handleClick = vi.fn();
  render(<Button onClick={handleClick}>Click me</Button>);
  
  await userEvent.click(screen.getByRole("button"));
  expect(handleClick).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
});
```

## 3. State Management Testing

### 3.1 RTK Testing
```tsx
import { configureStore } from "@reduxjs/toolkit";
import authReducer, { setUser } from "./authSlice";

describe("Auth Slice", () => {
  let store;

  beforeEach(() => {
    store = configureStore({
      reducer: { auth: authReducer },
    });
  });

  it("handles user login", () => {
    const user = { id: 1, name: "Test User" };
    store.dispatch(setUser(user));
    expect(store.getState().auth.user).toEqual(user);
  });
});
```

### 3.2 Zustand Testing
```tsx
import { renderHook, act } from "@testing-library/react";
import useStore from "./store";

describe("Zustand Store", () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    useStore.getState().reset();
  });

  it("updates theme", () => {
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useStore());
    act(() => {
      result.current.setTheme("dark");
    });
    expect(result.current.theme).toBe("dark");
  });
});
```

## 4. API and Data Fetching Tests

### 4.1 RTK Query Testing
```tsx
vi.mock("@/common/services/custom.api", () => ({
  useGetDataQuery: vi.fn(() => ({
    data: [],
    isLoading: false,
    isError: false,
  })),
}));
```

### 4.2 Custom Hooks Testing
```tsx
import { renderHook } from "@testing-library/react";
import { useData } from "./useData";

describe("useData hook", () => {
  it("returns initial state", () => {
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useData());
    expect(result.current.data).toBeNull();
    expect(result.current.isLoading).toBe(true);
  });
});
```

## 5. Test Utilities and Setup

### 5.1 Custom Render Function
```tsx
import { render } from "@testing-library/react";
import { Provider } from "react-redux";
import { configureStore } from "@reduxjs/toolkit";

const customRender = (ui: React.ReactElement, options = {}) => {
  const store = configureStore({
    reducer: {
      // Add your reducers here
    },
  });

  return render(
    <Provider store={store}>
      {ui}
    </Provider>,
    options
  );
};
```

### 5.2 Common Test Utilities
```tsx
// test-utils.ts
export const mockApiResponse = (data: any) => ({
  data,
  isLoading: false,
  isError: false,
  refetch: vi.fn(),
});

export const mockErrorResponse = (error: any) => ({
  data: null,
  isLoading: false,
  isError: true,
  error,
});
```

## 6. Best Practices

### 6.1 Test Organization
- Keep tests close to the code they test
- Use descriptive test names
- Group related tests using `describe` blocks
- Follow consistent naming conventions

### 6.2 Test Quality
- Test one thing at a time
- Avoid testing implementation details
- Use meaningful assertions
- Keep tests independent
- Clean up after tests

### 6.3 Performance
- Mock expensive operations
- Use `vi.useFakeTimers()` for time-dependent tests
- Avoid unnecessary renders
- Clean up resources in `afterEach`

## 7. Configuration

### 7.1 Vitest Config
```ts
// vitest.config.ts
export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    globals: true,
    environment: "jsdom",
    setupFiles: ["./src/test-utils/setup.ts"],
    coverage: {
      provider: "v8",
      reporter: ["text", "json", "html"],
      thresholds: {
        lines: 80,
        functions: 80,
        branches: 80,
        statements: 80,
      },
    },
  },
});
```

### 7.2 Test Scripts
```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "test": "vitest",
    "test:watch": "vitest watch",
    "test:coverage": "vitest run --coverage",
    "test:ui": "vitest --ui"
  }
}
```

## 8. Common Pitfalls to Avoid

- Over-mocking
- Testing implementation details
- Not cleaning up after tests
- Using too many snapshots
- Testing third-party libraries
- Not testing error cases
- Writing flaky tests
- Circular mocking: Don't mock the same response you're evaluating. If you're testing a controller or service, don't mock its exact output to verify the test. This creates a circular reference that doesn't actually test the implementation.

  ```tsx
  // BAD PRACTICE - Circular mocking
  it("getUser controller returns user data", async () => {
    // Mocking the exact response we want to test
    const mockUserData = { id: 1, name: "John" };
    getUserService.getUser = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(mockUserData);
    
    // This test will always pass because we're mocking the exact output
    const result = await getUserController.getUser(1);
    expect(result).toEqual(mockUserData);
  });
  
  // GOOD PRACTICE - Mock dependencies, not the controller itself
  it("getUser controller returns formatted user data", async () => {
    // Mock the lower-level service that the controller depends on
    const mockRawUserData = { userId: 1, userName: "John" };
    userRepository.fetchUser = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(mockRawUserData);
    
    // Test that the controller transforms the data correctly
    const result = await getUserController.getUser(1);
    expect(result).toEqual({ id: 1, name: "John" });
  });
  ```

## 9. Debugging Tests

### 9.1 Using Vitest UI
```bash
pnpm run test:ui
```

### 9.2 Debugging Tips
- Use `console.log` strategically
- Use `screen.debug()` to see rendered output
- Check test coverage reports
- Use `--inspect` flag for Node.js debugging

